WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:07.672
One afternoon Milly Snow visited Aunt Polly.

2
00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:12.694
"I came to find out how Pollyanna is doing," Milly said.

3
00:00:12.695 --> 00:00:16.757
Aunt Polly pushed back a loose strand of hair.

4
00:00:16.758 --> 00:00:20.654
"About the same, and how is your mother?"

5
00:00:20.655 --> 00:00:23.807
"That's what I want you to tell Pollyanna.

6
00:00:23.808 --> 00:00:29.959
Mother is so much better, and it's all thanks to Pollyanna and her game."

7
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:34.830
Aunt Polly wanted to ask about the game, but Milly kept on talking.

8
00:00:34.831 --> 00:00:39.584
"Mother just used to sit in her dark room and complain.

9
00:00:39.585 --> 00:00:46.342
But now she keeps the curtains open and takes an interest in her appearance."

10
00:00:46.343 --> 00:00:48.736
"That's nice."

11
00:00:48.737 --> 00:00:57.188
"After Pollyanna told Mother she should be glad she has arms and hands, Mother wanted to do something useful.

12
00:00:57.189 --> 00:01:05.142
So she knits blankets for charity, and her room is full of brightly colored yarn.

13
00:01:05.143 --> 00:01:12.490
I used to hate to go in there, but now I'm glad to. Anyway . . ." Milly took a deep breath.

14
00:01:12.491 --> 00:01:19.261
"We thought if Pollyanna knew she'd changed our lives, she might be glad."

15
00:01:19.262 --> 00:01:25.039
Milly stood up to go. "So will you tell her?"

16
00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:32.407
"Of course," Aunt Polly said, though she wasn't quite sure what Milly had been talking about.

17
00:01:32.408 --> 00:01:37.953
Many other visitors left mysterious messages for Pollyanna.

18
00:01:37.954 --> 00:01:42.351
When Widow Benton arrived, she was dressed in black as usual.

19
00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:46.077
But she was also wearing a blue ribbon around her neck.

20
00:01:46.078 --> 00:01:52.238
"Please tell Pollyanna about my ribbon," Widow Benton said to Aunt Polly.

21
00:01:52.239 --> 00:01:59.177
"I hope she'll be glad I've taken her suggestion to wear some color."

22
00:01:59.178 --> 00:02:03.658
That same day a stranger named Mrs. Tarbell arrived.

23
00:02:03.659 --> 00:02:07.849
She, too, was dressed in black, as if in mourning.

24
00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:13.725
"I've been staying at the hotel in town and taking long walks every day for my health.

25
00:02:13.726 --> 00:02:17.791
I always enjoyed walking with Pollyanna.

26
00:02:17.792 --> 00:02:23.390
She reminded me of my daughter who died years ago.

27
00:02:23.391 --> 00:02:29.474
Could you just tell her that I'm glad now? I'd rather not explain why."

28
00:02:29.475 --> 00:02:34.406
After Mrs. Tarbell left, Aunt Polly hurried upstairs.

29
00:02:34.407 --> 00:02:39.053
"Pollyanna, do you know a Mrs. Tarbell?"

30
00:02:39.054 --> 00:02:44.009
"Oh, yes. She's awfully sick and sad.

31
00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:47.131
We go for long walks together.

32
00:02:47.132 --> 00:02:55.747
I mean, we used to . . ." Pollyanna's voice broke, and two big tears rolled down her cheeks.

33
00:02:55.748 --> 00:03:03.751
Aunt Polly cleared her throat. "She said to tell you she's glad now."

34
00:03:03.752 --> 00:03:10.986
Pollyanna clapped her hands and almost smiled. "Oh, I'm so glad!"

35
00:03:10.987 --> 00:03:16.307
"She said something about a game. What was she talking about?"

36
00:03:16.308 --> 00:03:22.611
"Nothing." Pollyanna turned her head away. "I can't talk about it."

37
00:03:22.612 --> 00:03:28.704
Pollyanna seemed so upset that Aunt Polly left her alone.

38
00:03:28.705 --> 00:03:33.075
She went downstairs to the kitchen, where Nancy was ironing.

39
00:03:33.076 --> 00:03:39.378
"Nancy! All of Pollyanna's visitors want me to tell her they're playing some game.

40
00:03:39.379 --> 00:03:44.980
Half the town is wearing bright colors or doing new things all because of Pollyanna.

41
00:03:44.981 --> 00:03:48.569
I tried to ask her about it, but she wouldn't tell me."

42
00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:55.767
Aunt Polly stamped her foot. "What is this absurd game everyone's playing?"

43
00:03:55.768 --> 00:04:01.807
To Aunt Polly's surprise and dismay, Nancy burst into tears.

44
00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:08.450
When Nancy had calmed down, she told the story of the doll and the crutches in the donation box.

45
00:04:08.451 --> 00:04:16.473
"She was glad for crutches?" Aunt Polly choked back a sob.

46
00:04:16.474 --> 00:04:21.122
"But why wouldn't she tell me about the Glad Game?"

47
00:04:21.123 --> 00:04:25.841
Nancy picked up the napkin she'd just ironed and wrung it like a wet rag.

48
00:04:25.842 --> 00:04:30.262
"Begging your pardon, ma'am, but you wouldn't let her.

49
00:04:30.263 --> 00:04:36.259
You told her not to speak of her father, and it was his game.

50
00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:44.724
Pollyanna desperately wanted to play it, so she told a few people, and the game spread throughout the town.

51
00:04:44.725 --> 00:04:50.984
She was always so cheerful . . ." Nancy tried to smooth the wrinkled napkin.

52
00:04:50.985 --> 00:04:55.100
"Now everyone is sad she isn't glad anymore."

53
00:04:55.101 --> 00:05:01.176
"Well, I know someone who'll play that game with her right now!"

54
00:05:01.177 --> 00:05:04.904
Aunt Polly hurried back upstairs to Pollyanna's room.

55
00:05:04.905 --> 00:05:11.520
When she told Pollyanna that Nancy had explained the game to her, Pollyanna's face lit up with joy.

56
00:05:11.521 --> 00:05:17.306
"Oh, Aunt Polly, you're the person I've most wanted to play the Glad Game with!"

57
00:05:17.307 --> 00:05:22.507
Pollyanna held out her arms, and Aunt Polly hugged her.

58
00:05:22.508 --> 00:05:29.735
"Do you have any idea what you've accomplished?" Aunt Polly smiled broadly.

59
00:05:29.736 --> 00:05:36.315
"The whole town is happier because you taught everyone the Glad Game."

60
00:05:36.316 --> 00:05:39.348
Pollyanna suddenly looked serious.

61
00:05:39.349 --> 00:05:49.826
"I'm so glad I had legs that worked. Because without them, I couldn't have done that!"

